  <title>Accounts configuration</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Administration</gui><gui>Accounts configuration</gui></guiseq>
  shows the chart of accounts as a tree: assets, equities, expenses, revenue
  and liabilities, each with the accounts under it. <gui>Expand all</gui> and
  <gui>Collapse all</gui> open and close the tree, and <gui>Report hub</gui>
  exports it; see <link xref="report_hub"/>.</p>

  <section id="new">
  <title>Adding an account</title>
  <steps>
    <item><p>Select the account the new one goes under. It is shown as the
    <gui>Parent Account :</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Under <gui>Create new account</gui>, type its name and number.
    The first digit of the number decides its kind: 1 assets, 2 equities, 3
    expenses, 4 revenue, 5 liabilities.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Save</gui>.</p></item>
  </steps>
  <p>Right click an account and choose <gui>Edit account</gui> to change its
  number or move it under another parent. The top level accounts cannot be
  changed.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="selectable">
  <title>Selectable accounts</title>
  <p>Select an account and check what it may be used for, so it is offered in
  the windows concerned: expenses on vendor invoices, inventory, product
  revenue, writing checks, deposits, bank statements, cash on hand, or credit
  card payments. Only an account with no accounts under it can be
  selectable.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="delete">
  <title>Deleting an account</title>
  <p><gui>Delete</gui> removes the selected account. When it cannot, the
  button says why: <gui>Top level account</gui>, <gui>Has child
  account</gui>, <gui>Account used in configuration</gui>, or because entries
  have already been posted to it.</p>
  </section>

</page>
